  // We want to do input [6x7] dot weight^T [7x7] -> [6x7]
  // So transpose weight to [7x7] (actually same shape), but we want contracting dims: input dim 1 and weight dim 1
  // Actually, PyTorch Linear does x @ weight.T + bias, so weight.T shape [7x7]
  // So dot_general with lhs_contracting_dimensions=[1], rhs_contracting_dimensions=[1], batching dims empty
  // But weight is [7x7], so weight.T is transpose(weight) with permutation [1,0]
