  // PyTorch Conv3d default dimension_numbers: NCDHW (batch, channels, depth, height, width)
  // StableHLO convolution dimension_numbers: lhs = [b, i, d, h, w], rhs = [o, i, kd, kh, kw], output = [b, o, d_out, h_out, w_out]
  // Here:
  // lhs: %arg2: tensor<6x3x7x8x8xf32>
  // rhs: %arg0: tensor<7x3x3x3x3xf32>
  // output: tensor<6x7x5x6x6xf32> (calculated below)
